 ```
 
 Read the reported finish reason: an output/context limit or cancellation can truncate the JSON.
+
+## KVMem historical GC in the integrated server
+
+The KVMem integration in `ninfer-serve` provides `--kvmem-gc-lru` and
+`--kvmem-gc-redundancy` (the latter requires `--kvmem-query-scorer meanq-cosine`).
+Both currently require one GPU, one running request and RAM history; GC with SSD
+or multiple GPUs is rejected. The active working-set budget remains independent.
+
+`--kvmem-gc-aux-mib N` sets a separate positive shared allocation budget for GC
+directories, queues, retained old owners, feature banks, comparison edges and
+GC-specific producer scratch. The default with GC enabled is 1024 MiB; supplying
+the option without a GC policy is rejected. Native KV payload remains under
+`--kvmem-host-mib`. Neither account is a bound on whole-process RSS, model weights,
+other engine statistics/workspace or thread stacks. A small auxiliary quota can
+reject a request even when KV payload capacity is available.
+
+`/props` reports `kvmem.gc_policy`, configured `gc_aux_budget_bytes`, and usage
+fields `gc_aux_budget_bytes`, `gc_aux_bytes`, `gc_aux_peak_bytes`, `gc_aux_denied`.
+Failed initialization does not publish a half-created GC domain. A disabled policy,
+failed/stopped worker or insufficient auxiliary budget terminates the affected
+request through `service_unavailable` rather than silently selecting another
+policy. A stream that already started reports its terminal error in the stream.
+These counters describe allocator requests and retained capacity, not OS pages.
